# Xcode
.DS_Store
build/
*.pbxuser
!default.pbxuser
*.mode1v3
!default.mode1v3
*.mode2v3
!default.mode2v3
*.perspectivev3
!default.perspectivev3
xcuserdata/
*.xccheckout
*.moved-aside
DerivedData
*.hmap
*.ipa
*.xcuserstate

# Swift Package Manager
.build/
# xcodebuild -clonedSourcePackagesDirPath target (CI caches this; see .github/workflows/tests.yml)
.spm-checkouts/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
Package.pins

# CocoaPods
Pods/

# Carthage
Carthage/Build/

# Claude settings
.claude/*

# Dev tooling — keep local, don't push
.claude/*
.cursor/

# …but DO track project rule docs (loaded as guidance; belong in the repo)
!.claude/rules/
# …and DO track the workflows. `.github/` on its own silently swallowed a new workflow file:
# ignore rules do not apply to already-tracked files, so the existing ones kept working while
# anything added later vanished from the commit that added it. Excluding the contents rather than
# the directory is what lets the negation below be heard at all.
.github/*
!.github/workflows/
.impeccable.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
impeccable-style-universal/

# XcodeGen — regenerate locally: ./Scripts/generate-xcodeproj.sh
OpenGlasses.xcodeproj/
xcschemes-backup/
project.local.yml
.openglasses-generate.env

# Local secrets — private keys, never commit (the .example is the template)
secrets/*
!secrets/*.example
Config/Entitlements/Personal/*.entitlements
!Config/Entitlements/Personal/*.entitlements.example
# Meta DAT credentials live in project.local.yml (ignored above) as build settings substituted
# into the committed Info.plist. The old Config/Info/Info.personal.plist override is gone — a
# whole-plist copy went stale (ITMS-90683) and later swallowed those credentials.
Config/Info/Info.personal.plist

# Xcode user data (don't track)
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.pbxproj.backup

# Xcode Cloud post-clone tool downloads (XcodeGen release)
.ci-tools/

# MediaPipe Tasks binaries — fetched by Scripts/fetch-mediapipe-frameworks.sh (too large
# to commit: the graph static libraries exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit)
Vendor/MediaPipeTasks/Frameworks/

# llama.cpp engine (Plan DZ) — the xcframework itself is committed, as SherpaOnnx's is: a clone
# builds the app without first spending four minutes compiling an inference engine. The pin and
# the digests are tracked beside it (Vendor/LlamaCpp/{REVISION,SHA256SUMS,BUILD-INFO}), and the
# engine-reproducibility workflow rebuilds from the pinned sources to prove the committed bytes
# are still the ones those sources produce. `.build/` holds the upstream checkout, the cmake
# build trees, and the digests of whatever build last ran here.
Vendor/LlamaCpp/.build/

# Local TLS material — never commit private keys
*.crt
*.key
# Throwaway DerivedData for headless builds. `.dd-agent/` was the first; the glob covers the
# per-configuration ones a verification matrix needs (.dd-relsim, .dd-reldev, .dd-device …) so a
# parallel build's output can never be picked up by `git add`.
.dd-*/
